Z||000000||Denise||11-11-2000||04:48 PM||||Hi list!! been awhile!! <BR>The Fiero Store insists the 5spd 4 cyl HD clutch for the Iszsu Transmission will handle my 2.8  This is about to go in my car this week.  The Borg Warner that's in the car now, failed, only 18,000 miles! duh..  We won't know what the cause was until it's apart,  but I think the TO bearing is wedged in the clutch fingers. <P>Only thing I can determine so far is:  the TO bearing for the Iszsu trans is too small for the fingers on the larger 4spd w/2.8 clutch. I'm hearing various people tell me to use the larger clutch with the Iszsu trans. Fiero Store of couse says "use this" the HD 4cyl clutch.<BR>The big question is this:   How do I find a TO bearing that is large enough to not wedge through the clutch fingers?  <BR>Surely this is not unique to my car, allot of people use the Iszsu Trans even with the SBC.  I've not heard back from Archie about what clutch he's used.  And the Fiero shop was ok, but I had already dealt with the Fiero store.    INPUT PLEASE?? no, i'm not  going to race. just drive.. <BR>thanks allot  <BR>Denise,  ||||reg||1
